{
  "name": "Ember of Restoration",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/fire/projectile-arrow-fire-orange-yellow.webp",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><strong>Ember of Restoration.</strong> You keep a little piece of the forge’s warmth with you at all times.</p><ul><li><p>When a creature spends one or more Body dice during a <strong>a Soma Break</strong> while you tend to them with tools, bandages, or quiet ritual, that creature regains an extra amount of Integrity equal to your <strong>Body value</strong> (minimum 1) once per Soma Break.</p></li><li><p>You can apply this benefit to a number of creatures per Soma Break equal to your tier.</p></li></ul><p>This is the beginning of the Soul-Smith’s reputation as someone whose campfire is where people go to actually get better.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
